# Accepted Trivy findings for lab/demo AWS architecture.
# Each entry documents why the finding is accepted rather than suppressed globally.

# ALB HTTP listener (port 80) is used because no custom domain / ACM certificate is provisioned yet.
# Mitigated by restricting ALB SG ingress to CloudFront Managed Prefix List and requiring X-Origin-Verify header.
AVD-AWS-0054

# ALB must be internet-facing (internal = false) for CloudFront custom origin connectivity.
# Direct internet access is blocked by CloudFront origin-facing prefix list + X-Origin-Verify header.
AVD-AWS-0053

# CloudFront WAF (AWS WAFv2) is omitted to keep lab costs minimal.
AVD-AWS-0011

# CloudWatch Log Groups use default AWS-managed encryption instead of a customer-managed KMS key to avoid extra CMK costs.
AVD-AWS-0017

# ECS tasks in private subnets require outbound 0.0.0.0/0 egress (via NAT Gateway) for ECR, Secrets Manager, and CloudWatch.
AVD-AWS-0104

# Frontend S3 bucket uses SSE-S3 (AES256) instead of KMS CMK to keep CloudFront OAC setup simple and cost-free.
AVD-AWS-0132
